---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site collects and who it shares with.">

  <div class="page">
    <PageHeader title="Privacy" description="A short, plain account of what this site collects and who it shares with." />

    <section aria-labelledby="newsletter-heading">
      <h2 id="newsletter-heading">Newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        If you subscribe via the form on <a href="/blog">/blog</a> or at the end of a post,
        your email address is sent to <a href="https://buttondown.com" rel="noopener">Buttondown</a>,
        which stores it and delivers new posts to you by email. I don't run my own
        mailing infrastructure. Buttondown sends a confirmation email before adding you
        to the list (double opt-in), and every email it sends includes a one-click
        unsubscribe link. Buttondown's own privacy policy covers what they do with
        subscriber data.
      </p>
      <p>
        To delete your address, use the unsubscribe link in any email or write to
        <a href="/api/contact">hello@mjrossi.com</a> and I'll remove you.
      </p>
      <p>
        You don't have to use the form at all. <a href="/blog/rss.xml">RSS</a> reaches the
        same posts and tells me nothing about you, and if you'd rather not hand your
        address to a third party, email <a href="/api/contact">hello@mjrossi.com</a> and
        I'll add you to the list by hand.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="turnstile-heading">
      <h2 id="turnstile-heading">Anti-spam</h2>
      <p>
        The signup form uses <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/products/turnstile/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Turnstile</a>
        to block automated submissions. Turnstile is a CAPTCHA replacement that doesn't
        set tracking cookies and is designed not to require user-identifying signals.
        It runs only where that form is rendered — the blog index and the foot of each
        post — and nowhere else on the site. This is the disclosure the form's own fine
        print used to carry; it lives here now, and the form links to this page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="hosting-heading">
      <h2 id="hosting-heading">Hosting and logs</h2>
      <p>
        This site is served by Cloudflare Workers. Cloudflare receives the standard
        request metadata any web host receives (IP address, user agent, requested URL)
        and applies its own DDoS and security protections. I don't run analytics,
        third-party trackers, or advertising on the site. There are no cookies set by
        this site.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="changes-heading">
      <h2 id="changes-heading">Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this changes, it'll change here. Questions: <a href="/api/contact">hello@mjrossi.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>

</Base>
